#: ../../source/balanced-match_README.md:39
msgid ""
"For the first non-nested matching pair of `a` and `b` in `str`, return an"
" object with those keys:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/balanced-match_README.md:42
msgid "**start** the index of the first match of `a`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/balanced-match_README.md:43
msgid "**end** the index of the matching `b`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/balanced-match_README.md:44
msgid "**pre** the preamble, `a` and `b` not included"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/balanced-match_README.md:45
msgid "**body** the match, `a` and `b` not included"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/balanced-match_README.md:46
msgid "**post** the postscript, `a` and `b` not included"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/balanced-match_README.md:48
#: ../../source/balanced-match_README.md:57
msgid "If there's no match, `undefined` will be returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/balanced-match_README.md:50
msgid ""
"If the `str` contains more `a` than `b` / there are unmatched pairs, the "
"first match that was closed will be used. For example, `{{a}` will match "
"`['{', 'a', '']` and `{a}}` will match `['', 'a', '}']`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/balanced-match_README.md:52
msgid "var r = balanced.range(a, b, str)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/balanced-match_README.md:54
msgid ""
"For the first non-nested matching pair of `a` and `b` in `str`, return an"
" array with indexes: `[ <a index>, <b index> ]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/balanced-match_README.md:59
msgid ""
"If the `str` contains more `a` than `b` / there are unmatched pairs, the "
"first match that was closed will be used. For example, `{{a}` will match "
"`[ 1, 3 ]` and `{a}}` will match `[0, 2]`."
msgstr ""

